35. Now, comes the question as to whether police authority can render any such help without a case being instituted by the Patna High Court MJC No.895 of 2025 dt.18-07-2025 petitioner/wife?
In light of the special circumstances in the present case that: (a) since marriage,
the petitioner has been in occupation of the first floor;
(b) the premises in her occupation was separate from the premises in occupation of the respondents;
(c) the subsistence of an injunction order in this very suit, restraining the petitioner from disturbing the possession of the respondents of the ground floor;
(d) the fact that this order has not been violated by the petitioner;
Patna High Court MJC No.895 of 2025 dt.18-07-2025 (e) the petitioner being pushed to file Execution Petitions to obtain the maintenance awarded to her;
(f) the application moved by the petitioner for payment of the electricity charges in respect of the first floor of the premises where the petitioner is residing and the claim of the respondent No.2 that he did not have the means to do so;
(g) the uncertainty, in these circumstances of the respondents meeting their obligation of paying rent regularly, and (h) finally, the prevailing circumstances of the pandemic when such an order was passed, all reflect the perversity and unreasonableness of the impugned order.
